        stepCount = 7,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Buy the crafted toy or level Engineering and its specialization to make it; activating the teleport remains profession-gated.\n\n1. For collection only, search the Auction House for the finished Dimensional Ripper - Area 52 (30542), or ask a Goblin Engineer to make it. You can add the finished toy without Engineering; buying it does not let an ineligible character teleport. If you obtain one this way, continue at step 7.\n\n2. For self-crafting, reach Classic Engineering 200 and choose the Goblin specialization. At level 20 or higher, take Goblin Engineering (29475) from Lilliam Sparkspindle in Stormwind (62.8, 32.0) or Roxxik in Orgrimmar (56.8, 56.4). Bring 20 Big Iron Bombs, 20 Solid Dynamite and 5 Explosive Sheep to complete it. Bought quest items work too. Skip this if you are already a Goblin Engineer.\n\n3. Learn Outland Engineering from Lebowski outside the Honor Hold keep in Hellfire Peninsula (55.6, 65.6, Alliance) or Zebig in Thrallmar (54.8, 38.4, Horde). Raise that expansion's Engineering skill to 50. Classic Engineering and Outland Engineering are separate bars; the old comments' 350 requirement is not 350 points in the current Outland profession.\n\n4. Visit Kablamm Farflinger beside the transporter in Area 52, Netherstorm (32.8, 63.6). Speak to him and select the dialogue asking how to make the dangerous dimensional device. He teaches the recipe directly when you have Goblin Engineering and Outland Engineering 50. He is not beside the town's ordinary Engineering trainer, and there is no schematic item to buy from a vendor list.\n\n5. Gather the recipe's actual components: 1 Adamantite Frame, 2 Primal Fire, 2 The Bigger One bombs, 4 Handfuls of Fel Iron Bolts and 1 Khorium Power Core. Buy finished components or make them with Outland Engineering. The Bigger One is a batch craft, so you can have a spare bomb; several older raw-material shopping lists also confuse Arcane Dust with Arcane Powder or use obsolete Khorium totals.\n\n6. Stand at an anvil, open Outland Engineering and craft Dimensional Ripper - Area 52. If it is missing, clear the Have Materials filter and check that you learned the recipe through Kablamm's dialogue. Raising Outland Engineering to 50 without the Goblin specialization does not unlock it.\n\n7. Use the finished item from your bags to add it to the account-wide Toy Box. To activate the teleport afterwards, use a Goblin Engineer with Outland Engineering 50. It can put you on a floating rock above Area 52 instead of the pad: arrive with a usable flying mount or another way to leave safely, and do not jump off without fall protection.",
