        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Buy the crafted toy or level Engineering and its specialization to make it; activating the teleport remains profession-gated.\n\n1. For collection only, buy the finished Ultrasafe Transporter: Toshley's Station (30544) on the Auction House or ask a Gnomish Engineer to craft it. A non-engineer can add it to the Toy Box, although using the teleport still requires the profession and specialization. If you obtain the finished toy, continue at step 7.\n\n2. For self-crafting, reach Classic Engineering 200 and choose the Gnomish specialization. At level 20 or higher, take Gnomish Engineering (29477) from Lilliam Sparkspindle in Stormwind (62.8, 32.0) or Roxxik in Orgrimmar (56.8, 56.4). Turn in 6 Mithril Tubes, 2 Advanced Target Dummies and 1 Accurate Scope. You can buy these items. Skip this if you are already a Gnomish Engineer.\n\n3. Train Outland Engineering with Lebowski outside the Honor Hold keep in Hellfire Peninsula (55.6, 65.6, Alliance) or Zebig in Thrallmar (54.8, 38.4, Horde), then raise Outland Engineering to 50. The old unsplit Engineering 350 figure in comments became Outland Engineering 50; skill in a different expansion does not satisfy it.\n\n4. Find Smiles O'Byron at the transporter pad NORTH of Toshley's Station in Blade's Edge Mountains (60.2, 65.2), near the graveyard. Speak to him and choose the dialogue about building a beacon to learn the recipe for free. You need Gnomish Engineering and Outland Engineering 50. Both factions can speak to Smiles; Horde characters should stay at the pad outside the Alliance settlement.\n\n5. Collect 1 Adamantite Frame, 2 Primal Air, 2 Felsteel Stabilizers, 4 Handfuls of Fel Iron Bolts and 1 Khorium Power Core. Buy the components or craft them. If making the two Felsteel Stabilizers yourself, they require 4 Felsteel Bars in total; do not mistake those for Khorium Bars in the older comments.\n\n6. At an anvil, open Outland Engineering and craft Ultrasafe Transporter - Toshley's Station. The recipe uses a hyphen while the finished toy uses a colon. Clear the Have Materials filter if the recipe is hidden, and revisit Smiles's dialogue if you have not learned it. Toshley himself does not teach this recipe.\n\n7. Use the finished item from your bags to learn the account-wide toy. An eligible Gnomish Engineer with Outland Engineering 50 can then activate it from the Toy Box. The normal arrival is the pad beside Smiles, outside the station. Malfunctions can cause appearance changes or a temporary chicken transformation; wait for the effect to end if it prevents normal actions.",
