        stepCount = 12,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Complete Toshley's Alliance quest chain, including any unfinished unlocks and its special quest-item mechanics.\n\n1. Use an Alliance character of at least level 20 and enable Trivial Quests in the minimap tracking options. Visit Toshley at Toshley's Station in Blade's Edge Mountains (60.5, 69.0). If he offers Picking Up Some Power Converters, skip the optional unlock in steps 2-6 and continue at step 7. If you already have a later quest, resume at its step below. Horde can use the collected toy but cannot earn it from their version of the Razaan quest.\n\n2. OPTIONAL UNLOCK: If Toshley offers nothing, visit Commander Skyshadow in Sylvanaar (36.5, 66.4). Complete The Bloodmaul Ogres (10502): kill 30 Bloodmaul ogres around Bloodmaul Outpost (45.0, 75.0), then return. Take The Bladespire Ogres (10504), kill 30 ogres in Bladespire Hold/Bladespire Grounds around 42.0, 51.0 and return again. The ogres at Bladespire Outpost near Toshley's Station are the wrong camp for this second quest.\n\n3. OPTIONAL UNLOCK: Speak to Vindicator Vuuleen in the cage at Bladespire Hold (44.0, 51.8). Take The Trappings of a Vindicator (10516). Kill Droggam in his building near 38.5, 52.5 and loot her Blade; kill Mugdorg in the building near 42.4, 58.6 and loot her Shield. Return both to Vuuleen. A strong legacy-farming character can clear their guards rather than reproduce old class-specific tricks.\n\n4. OPTIONAL UNLOCK: Take Gorr'Dim, Your Time Has Come... (10517) from Vuuleen. Kill Gorr'Dim inside the large building near 39.5, 49.8, then return to her and accept Planting the Banner (10518). Do not leave the chain after merely recovering the sword and shield.\n\n5. OPTIONAL UNLOCK: Kill a Bladespire Champion near 41.3, 46.8 for the Bladespire Clan Banner. Go south to the top of Northmaul Tower at Bloodmaul Outpost (46.5, 74.4), use the banner and defeat the attacking waves, followed by Gurn Grubnosh. Loot his Helm. If another player's banner is already there, let their event finish and the banner disappear before placing yours.\n\n6. OPTIONAL UNLOCK: Return to Commander Skyshadow in Sylvanaar to finish Planting the Banner and take Where Did Those Darn Gnomes Go? (10580). Find R-3D0 at the foot of the ridge west of Toshley's Station (55.0, 72.8), turn it in and accept Follow the Breadcrumbs (10581). Follow the spare-parts trail up the ramp to Toshley (60.5, 69.0) and turn that in to open his quests.\n\n7. Accept Picking Up Some Power Converters (10584) from Toshley. Go north to Bladespire Outpost around 57.5, 56.0. Click a Power Converter on the ground to release an Electromental, target the creature and use the provided Protovoltaic Magneto Collector BEFORE killing it. Kill it once it is encased. Repeat until 5 Electromentals are collected; dismiss attacking pets or stop automatic attacks if they kill it before the collector finishes.\n\n8. Return to Toshley and take Ride the Lightning (10657). Go to Scalewing Shelf east/southeast of the station, around 68.5, 72.0. Activate the provided Repolarized Magneto Sphere on yourself, aggro Scalewing Serpents and let their lightning hit you until the counter reaches 25. Leave the serpents alive while collecting strikes; a high-level character can body-pull them without attacking. Then kill enough to loot 5 Scalewing Lightning Glands and return to Toshley.\n\n9. Accept Trapping the Light Fantastic (10674). Travel to Razaan's Landing around 65.5, 43.2 and repeatedly place the provided Multi-Spectrum Light Trap beside the TINY PINK floating lights until you have trapped 15. These are not the large yellow souls that drift out of dead ethereals. Return to Toshley; this quest leads to the toy quest but does not itself award the toy.\n\n10. Take Show Them Gnome Mercy! (10675). Return to the portal apparatus with a tall pink tube at Razaan's Landing (66.4, 44.2). Kill the Razaani ethereals nearby. Their yellow souls travel slowly to the tube; keep clearing and allow them to arrive. When the apparatus fills and completes its animation, Nexus-Prince Razaan appears with a yell. Killing unrelated flesh beasts does not replace the ethereal souls.\n\n11. Kill Nexus-Prince Razaan, then click the separate runed BOX that appears above/near his body and take the Collection of Souls. The quest needs the item from that box, not just kill credit or ordinary corpse loot. Loot it promptly before it disappears. If someone else already killed the prince, a still-present box can supply the item while you have the quest.\n\n12. Return to Toshley at 60.5, 69.0 and turn in Show Them Gnome Mercy! Power Converter is an additional guaranteed reward alongside your equipment choice. Use the item from your bags to add it to the account-wide Toy Box. Eligible Horde alts can use it afterwards; the Horde quest There Can Be Only One Response does not award this toy.",
